{
  "id": "explore-time-series-display-options",
  "title": "Compare display options",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Explore finished panels that differ in one display option to see what interpolation, fill opacity, and stacking change."
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "compare-interpolation",
      "title": "Compare connecting lines",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "navigate",
          "reftarget": "/d/000000016/time-series-graphs?from=now-1h&to=now&timezone=browser&dtab=More-Examples",
          "verify": "on-page:/d/000000016",
          "content": "Open **Time series graphs** on its **More Examples** tab."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-589']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Find **Linear** in the **Interpolation** row."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Straight lines join the samples."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-590']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Smooth**."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Curves join the samples instead. The curves don't add measurements between them."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-591']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Step before**."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-592']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Step after**."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Both hold a value flat until the next sample, then jump. Step before puts the jump before each sample. Step after puts it after."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "compare-fill",
      "title": "Separate shading from magnitude",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-573']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Lines** again. Its fill opacity is 0, so there is no shading under the line."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-586']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Fill opacity = 10**. A faint shade sits under each line."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-testid='data-testid Tab Time Series Introduction']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "content": "Select the **Time Series Introduction** tab."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-1']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Simple graph**. Its fill opacity is 40."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "The shading is stronger, and where series overlap, one can hide another. The shading changes. The line positions don't. Darker fill doesn't mean a larger value."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "compare-stacking",
      "title": "What a boundary means",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-1']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Simple graph** again. It's unstacked, which is stacking **Off**."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Hover at one time and read its value. Each line is measured from zero."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-3']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Stacked lines**. Its stacking is **Normal**."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Hover at one time. Each series sits on top of the one below, so the top boundary is their total, not the top series' own value. Read individual values from the tooltip."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "The third mode, **100%**, isn't shown here. It rescales every point in time to 100 percent, so you see each series' share of the total and lose the total itself."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Stacking can mislead and hide data. The Grafana docs recommend turning it off in most cases."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
